{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# NumPyro NUTS vs Pyro Variational Inference for the Same BNN\n","\n","This notebook asks an operational question rather than only an inference question:\n","\n","> Does the posterior approximation method materially change uncertainty estimates and downstream decisions?\n","\n","The same small BNN family is fitted with:\n","\n","1. Pyro SVI + `AutoDiagonalNormal`,\n","2. NumPyro NUTS.\n","\n","The comparison includes RMSE, predictive coverage, interval width, inference time, and expected-cost / CVaR production decisions.\n","\n","NUTS is **not** treated as ground truth. Finite MCMC samples, convergence diagnostics, and model specification still matter.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import time, random, numpy as np, pandas as pd, matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import torch, torch.nn as nn, pyro, pyro.distributions as pydist\n","from pyro.infer import SVI, Trace_ELBO, Predictive as PyroPredictive\n","from pyro.infer.autoguide import AutoDiagonalNormal\n","from pyro.nn import PyroModule, PyroSample\n","import jax, jax.numpy as jnp, numpyro, numpyro.distributions as ndist\n","from numpyro.infer import MCMC, NUTS, Predictive as NumPyroPredictive\n","SEED=42\n","random.seed(SEED); np.random.seed(SEED); torch.manual_seed(SEED); pyro.set_rng_seed(SEED); torch.set_default_dtype(torch.float32)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Common synthetic demand dataset\n","\n","A temporal holdout is used so both inference methods are evaluated on the same future observations.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def demand_parameters(X):\n","    promo,weekend,temp,season,trend=[X[...,i] for i in range(5)]\n","    mu=105+18*promo+8*weekend+13*season+.45*temp+8*trend+5*promo*season\n","    return mu,7.0\n","n=260; day=np.arange(n); promo=np.random.binomial(1,.25,n).astype(np.float32); weekend=((day%7)>=5).astype(np.float32)\n","temp=(22+9*np.sin(2*np.pi*day/90)+np.random.normal(0,2,n)).astype(np.float32); season=np.sin(2*np.pi*day/30).astype(np.float32); trend=(day/(n-1)).astype(np.float32)\n","Xr=np.column_stack([promo,weekend,temp,season,trend]).astype(np.float32); mu,sig=demand_parameters(Xr); yr=(mu+np.random.normal(0,sig,n)).astype(np.float32)\n","ntr=200; Xtrr,Xter=Xr[:ntr],Xr[ntr:]; ytrr,yte=yr[:ntr],yr[ntr:]\n","Xm,Xs=Xtrr.mean(0,keepdims=True),Xtrr.std(0,keepdims=True)+1e-6; ym,ys=float(ytrr.mean()),float(ytrr.std()+1e-6)\n","Xtr=((Xtrr-Xm)/Xs).astype(np.float32); Xte=((Xter-Xm)/Xs).astype(np.float32); ytr=((ytrr-ym)/ys).astype(np.float32)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Same BNN specification in Pyro and NumPyro\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["H=6; D=Xtr.shape[1]\n","class PyroBNN(PyroModule):\n","    def __init__(self):\n","        super().__init__(); self.h=PyroModule[nn.Linear](D,H); self.o=PyroModule[nn.Linear](H,1)\n","        self.h.weight=PyroSample(pydist.Normal(0,.8).expand([H,D]).to_event(2)); self.h.bias=PyroSample(pydist.Normal(0,.8).expand([H]).to_event(1))\n","        self.o.weight=PyroSample(pydist.Normal(0,.8).expand([1,H]).to_event(2)); self.o.bias=PyroSample(pydist.Normal(0,.8).expand([1]).to_event(1))\n","    def forward(self,X,y=None):\n","        m=self.o(torch.tanh(self.h(X))).squeeze(-1); s=pyro.sample('sigma',pydist.LogNormal(-1,.35)); pyro.deterministic('mu',m)\n","        with pyro.plate('data',X.shape[0]): pyro.sample('obs',pydist.Normal(m,s),obs=y)\n","        return m\n","\n","def numpyro_bnn(X,y=None):\n","    W1=numpyro.sample('W1',ndist.Normal(0,.8).expand((H,D)).to_event(2)); b1=numpyro.sample('b1',ndist.Normal(0,.8).expand((H,)).to_event(1))\n","    W2=numpyro.sample('W2',ndist.Normal(0,.8).expand((1,H)).to_event(2)); b2=numpyro.sample('b2',ndist.Normal(0,.8).expand((1,)).to_event(1)); s=numpyro.sample('sigma',ndist.LogNormal(-1,.35))\n","    h=jnp.tanh(X@W1.T+b1); m=(h@W2.T).squeeze(-1)+b2.squeeze(-1); numpyro.deterministic('mu',m)\n","    with numpyro.plate('data',X.shape[0]): numpyro.sample('obs',ndist.Normal(m,s),obs=y)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Pyro mean-field VI\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["Xt=torch.tensor(Xtr); Xtt=torch.tensor(Xte); yt=torch.tensor(ytr)\n","pyro.clear_param_store(); pm=PyroBNN(); guide=AutoDiagonalNormal(pm); svi=SVI(pm,guide,pyro.optim.Adam({'lr':.01}),loss=Trace_ELBO())\n","t0=time.perf_counter(); losses=[]\n","for _ in range(3000): losses.append(svi.step(Xt,yt)/len(yt))\n","vi_time=time.perf_counter()-t0\n","vi=PyroPredictive(pm,guide=guide,num_samples=1500,return_sites=('obs','mu'))(Xtt)\n","vi_obs=vi['obs'].detach().numpy()*ys+ym; vi_mu=vi['mu'].detach().numpy()*ys+ym\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. NumPyro NUTS\n","\n","The pedagogical run uses one chain for runtime. A serious analysis should use multiple chains and inspect \(\\hat R\\), ESS, and divergences.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["kernel=NUTS(numpyro_bnn,target_accept_prob=.85,max_tree_depth=8); mcmc=MCMC(kernel,num_warmup=700,num_samples=1000,num_chains=1,progress_bar=True)\n","t0=time.perf_counter(); mcmc.run(jax.random.key(SEED),jnp.asarray(Xtr),jnp.asarray(ytr),extra_fields=('diverging',)); nuts_time=time.perf_counter()-t0\n","mcmc.print_summary(); print('Divergences:',int(np.asarray(mcmc.get_extra_fields()['diverging']).sum()))\n","post=mcmc.get_samples(); pred=NumPyroPredictive(numpyro_bnn,posterior_samples=post,return_sites=['obs','mu'])(jax.random.key(SEED+1),jnp.asarray(Xte))\n","nuts_obs=np.asarray(pred['obs'])*ys+ym; nuts_mu=np.asarray(pred['mu'])*ys+ym\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Predictive comparison\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def metrics(samples,truth):\n","    mean=samples.mean(0); lo,hi=np.quantile(samples,[.05,.95],axis=0)\n","    return {'RMSE':np.sqrt(np.mean((mean-truth)**2)),'coverage90':np.mean((truth>=lo)&(truth<=hi)),'mean_interval_width':np.mean(hi-lo),'mean_predictive_sd':np.mean(samples.std(0))}\n","table=pd.DataFrame([metrics(vi_obs,yte),metrics(nuts_obs,yte)],index=['Pyro VI','NumPyro NUTS']); table['inference_seconds']=[vi_time,nuts_time]; table.round(3)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Downstream production decision\n","\n","At one future condition, posterior predictive scenarios are converted into expected-cost and CVaR decisions through a one-dimensional search. This isolates the effect of posterior uncertainty on the decision.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["future=np.array([[1,1,31,.4,1.03]],dtype=np.float32); fscaled=((future-Xm)/Xs).astype(np.float32)\n","vi_future=PyroPredictive(pm,guide=guide,num_samples=4000,return_sites=('obs',))(torch.tensor(fscaled))['obs'].detach().numpy().reshape(-1)*ys+ym\n","nuts_future=NumPyroPredictive(numpyro_bnn,posterior_samples=post,return_sites=['obs'])(jax.random.key(SEED+2),jnp.asarray(fscaled))['obs']; nuts_future=np.asarray(nuts_future).reshape(-1)*ys+ym\n","c,h,p,alpha=1.,.3,5.,.95\n","def losses(x,D): return c*x+h*np.maximum(x-D,0)+p*np.maximum(D-x,0)\n","def choose(D,mode):\n","    grid=np.linspace(np.quantile(D,.15),np.quantile(D,.995),350); vals=[]\n","    for x in grid:\n","        L=losses(x,D)\n","        vals.append(L.mean() if mode=='mean' else L[L>=np.quantile(L,alpha)].mean())\n","    return float(grid[np.argmin(vals)])\n","rows=[]\n","for name,Dd in [('Pyro VI',vi_future),('NumPyro NUTS',nuts_future)]: rows.append({'method':name,'expected_cost_decision':choose(Dd,'mean'),'CVaR95_decision':choose(Dd,'cvar'),'predictive_q95':np.quantile(Dd,.95)})\n","pd.DataFrame(rows).round(2)\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Takeaway\n","\n","The important question is not whether NUTS is philosophically more Bayesian than VI. The useful question is whether the cheaper posterior approximation is calibrated well enough that it produces essentially the same decisions. If not, inference quality becomes an OR concern.\n"]}],"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.x"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}